  "description": "Lossless FLAC encoding for CodeBrix.Audio. FlacEncoder turns float or integer samples into a standard .flac stream - 4- to 32-bit samples, compression levels 0 to 8, optional verify-while-encoding, seek table, padding and Vorbis comments, with the stream totals and MD5 filled in when the destination can seek - and FlacPacketEncoder yields one FLAC frame per packet plus the stream header for containers. Built over self-built native libraries shipped in the package for Windows x64 and ARM64, macOS Intel and Apple Silicon, Linux x64, ARM64 and RISC-V 64, and Android 13+ ARM64 and x64. One Register() call lets CodeBrix.Audio write .flac files by file name.",
